E28F   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
E290   86 51        E_QUOTE:   LDA   #"Q"   ; " or $ ran into the NUL
E292                             ; and fall into error. (H, W and N have their own entries, near
E292                             ; their handlers, at ejmp.)
E292                             ; =============================================================================
E292                             ;  Checked build: the error report. A = the letter, AT = the place; U is
E292                             ;  as the program left it, and SSAV holds S as the failing character began
E292                             ;  (see "the error entries" after `upper`).
E292                             ;  It sits here, ahead of h_num, pdec and putc, so that it reaches them with
E292                             ;  short calls. Prints
E292                             ; 
E292                             ;     CR LF
E292                             ;     Err X @ line,col CR LF
E292                             ;     D:n:[ ...][ v]*  CR LF     (the top 8 cells, bottom to top, signed)
E292                             ;     R:n CR LF
E292                             ; 
E292                             ;  and goes to EXIT. Line and column count from 1: the line is one more
E292                             ;  than the LFs between PROG and the place, the column the distance from the
E292                             ;  last LF (or from PROG-1). A place below PROG is in the -n? line buffer:
E292                             ;  line 0, column = its offset there + 1. Numbers other than the cells are
E292                             ;  printed unsigned (pdec), the cells signed (h_num).
E292                             ; 
E292                             ;  The data stack may be one cell past its limit (S, U = 8100h): the
E292                             ;  report's own cells then reach 6 bytes further down, to 80FAh, into the
E292                             ;  return stack page, so the report runs on a fresh return stack at RSREP
E292                             ;  (80F0h), below those bytes.
E292                             ; =============================================================================
E292   10 CE 80 F0  ERROR:    LDS   #RSREP   
E296   1F 89                  TFR   A,B   ; the letter (pmsg and CONOUT keep B)
E298   8D 34                  BSR   pmsg   
E29A   0D 0A 45 72 72 A0      FCB   13,10,"Err"," "+80h   
E2A0   1F 98                  TFR   B,A   
E2A2   BD FF 03               JSR   CONOUT   
E2A5   8D 27                  BSR   pmsg   
E2A7   20 40 A0               FCB   " @"," "+80h   
E2AA                             ; the place: Y counts the lines, X walks, the cell at ,U holds the
E2AA                             ; address of the last LF (PROG-1 to begin with)
E2AA   10 8E 00 00            LDY   #0   
E2AE   8E 82 7F               LDX   #LINEBUF-1   
E2B1   36 10                  PSHU   X   
E2B3   8E 82 FF               LDX   #PROG-1   
E2B6   9C 36                  CMPX   <AT   
E2B8   24 23                  BHS   lc3   ; the place is below PROG: line 0
E2BA   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
E2BC   31 21        LC1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; a line
E2BE   30 01        LC2:      LEAX   1,X   
E2C0   9C 36                  CMPX   <AT   
E2C2   24 19                  BHS   lc3   
E2C4   A6 84                  LDA   ,X   
E2C6   81 0A                  CMPA   #10   
E2C8   26 F4                  BNE   lc2   
E2CA   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
E2CC   20 EE                  BRA   lc1   
E2CE                             ; pmsg: print the text after the call, up to and including the character
E2CE                             ; that has bit 7 set (it is printed without it), then return after it.
E2CE                             ; (It sits here, in the middle of the report, where all its calls reach.)
E2CE   35 10        PMSG:     PULS   X   
E2D0   A6 84        PM1:      LDA   ,X   
E2D2   84 7F                  ANDA   #7Fh   
E2D4   BD E3 61               JSR   putc   
E2D7   6D 80                  TST   ,X+   
E2D9   2A F5                  BPL   pm1   
E2DB   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
E2DD   DC 36        LC3:      LDD   <AT   
E2DF   A3 C4                  SUBD   ,U   
E2E1   ED C4                  STD   ,U   ; the column
E2E3   36 20                  PSHU   Y   
E2E5   8D 62                  BSR   pdec   ; the line
E2E7   8D E5                  BSR   pmsg   
E2E9   AC                     FCB   ","+80h   
E2EA   8D 5D                  BSR   pdec   ; the column
E2EC   8D E0                  BSR   pmsg   
E2EE   0D 0A 44 BA            FCB   13,10,"D",":"+80h   
E2F2                             ; the data stack: its depth, then its top 8 cells, from Y down to
E2F2                             ; the program's top cell, at ,U.
E2F2   34 40                  PSHS   U   ; where the walk ends
E2F4   CC 81 FC               LDD   #DSTOP   
E2F7   A3 E4                  SUBD   ,S   
E2F9   8D 3D                  BSR   pdh   ; the depth (pdec leaves U as it was)
E2FB   8D D1                  BSR   pmsg   
E2FD   BA                     FCB   ":"+80h   
E2FE   31 C8 10               LEAY   16,U   ; past the 8th cell from the top ...
E301   10 8C 81 FC            CMPY   #DSTOP   
E305   24 08                  BHS   sl1   
E307   8D C5                  BSR   pmsg   ; (there are more than 8)
E309   20 2E 2E AE            FCB   " ..","."+80h   
E30D   20 04                  BRA   sl2   
